   "note": "The problem asks for graph connectivity (reachability) on 6 nodes. Connectivity is a global property invariant under node relabeling. The ansatz block is designed to respect the cyclic symmetry of the node indices (0->1->2->3->4->5->0), which is a subgroup of the full symmetric group S6. The block consists of a linear chain of CNOTs (wrapping around to close the cycle), followed by single-qubit Z rotations, then the same CNOT chain again, followed by single-qubit Y rotations. The CNOT chains create entanglement along the cycle, allowing information to propagate between neighbors. The parameterized rotations introduce non-linearity and tunable phases/amplitudes. By tying the structure to the cyclic shift symmetry, we reduce the hypothesis space and potentially improve generalization for the connectivity task, assuming the feature map also respects this symmetry (which it does if the features are encoded in a way that commutes with the shift, or if the training learns to ignore the specific labeling). The block has 24 gates, 12 parameters. The hypothesis claims invariance under the cyclic permutation of qubits.",
